<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Karasahr</h1><p class="st-meta">200 BCE – 840 CE (approx.) · capital Karasahr</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The oasis kingdom of Agni on the northern Silk Road, one of the homes of the Tocharian languages and of Central Asian Buddhism.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karashahr">Karasahr</a>, called Yanqi in Chinese and Agni in its own documents, grew around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosten-lake">Bosten Lake</a> oasis on the north-eastern edge of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarim-basin">Tarim Basin</a>. It enters Chinese records in the 2nd century BCE as one of the city-states of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-regions">Western Regions</a>, alternating between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu</a> and Han control.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Its people spoke Tocharian A, an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indo-european-languages">Indo-European</a> language preserved in Buddhist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscripts</a>. Ruled by its own kings, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karashahr">Karasahr</a> lived from irrigated farming, fishing, salt and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk-road">Silk Road</a> trade, and its monasteries at Shikshin followed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarvastivada">Sarvastivada</a> school. The pilgrim <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xuanzang">Xuanzang</a> passed through in 630. The Han general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ban-chao">Ban Chao</a> subdued it in 94, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a> conquered it in 644 and made it one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/four-garrisons-of-anxi">Four Garrisons of Anxi</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/later-tang">Tang</a> power in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarim-basin">Tarim</a> faded in the late 8th century, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karashahr">Karasahr</a> passed under Tibetan and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uyghurs">Uyghur</a> influence. Uyghurs fleeing the fall of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/uyghur-khaganate">Uyghur Khaganate</a> in 840 settled there, and the region became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-qocho">Kingdom of Qocho</a>, where Tocharian gave way to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-uyghur-language">Old Uyghur</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 200 BCE – 840 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:55.72%;width:20.70%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>200 BCE – 840 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Karasahr</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Tocharian A</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/china">China</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Agni, Yanqi</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=320&amp;focus=kingdom-of-karasahr" aria-label="Kingdom of Karasahr on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6783 681 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Karasahr lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7103 937L7771 1192M7103 937L7137 873"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7771 1192h0M7137 873h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7103 937h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7103 937h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Karasahr. <a href="/atlas?year=320&amp;focus=kingdom-of-karasahr">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
